# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `job` object exists only in the notebook that started the run. In a new notebook, get the job again with `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, then call `runtime_jobs()` on it. See [Find a job from a new session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"
msgstr "Objekt `job` existuje pouze v notebooku, který běh spustil. V novém notebooku získej úlohu znovu pomocí `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")` a poté na ní zavolej `runtime_jobs()`. Viz [Najdi úlohu z nové session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the QPU usage and run times of each QPU job, see [View job metrics](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). For the usage of your whole instance in the current period, call `client.usage()`. To see how long each stage of the managed workflow job took, see [Check how long each stage took](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"
msgstr "Informace o využití QPU a dobách běhu každé úlohy na QPU najdeš v části [Zobrazení metrik úlohy](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). Využití celé své instance v aktuálním období zjistíš voláním `client.usage()`. Chceš-li zjistit, jak dlouho trvala každá fáze úlohy spravovaného workflow, viz [Zkontroluj, jak dlouho trvala každá fáze](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel linked QPU jobs {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"
msgstr "Zruš propojené úlohy na QPU {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Když zrušíš úlohu spravovaného workflow pomocí `job.cancel()`, workflow se také pokusí zrušit práci na QPU, kterou spustil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Session a batche.** Workflow zruší každou ze svých session a batchů, čímž zruší i jejich úlohy ve frontě.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Další primitivní úlohy.** Workflow zruší každou ze svých dalších primitivních úloh, které jsou stále ve frontě nebo běží.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` vrací zprávu pro každou úlohu na QPU a každou session, takže můžeš zkontrolovat, co bylo zrušeno:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "U workflow, který běžel v batch, vypadá zpráva takto:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Pokud klient nemůže z tvých lokálních přihlašovacích údajů vytvořit `QiskitRuntimeService`, zruší pouze úlohu spravovaného workflow. Úlohy na QPU zruš sám pomocí jejich ID z `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Když workflow zastaví úlohu sám, například proto, že dosáhla 24hodinového limitu, své úlohy na QPU nezruší. Zruš je pomocí jejich ID z `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Řešení potíží s úlohami na QPU ve workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problém | Příčina |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` vyvolá `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | Kód běží v tvém lokálním notebooku, ne v úloze spravovaného workflow. Lokálně použij `QiskitRuntimeService()`. |\n"
"| `update_status()` vrací `False` a logy ukazují `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | Hodnota není jednou z konstant `Job` nebo úloha již není aktivní. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` vrací `[]`. | Workflow vytvořil svou službu pomocí `QiskitRuntimeService()` nebo ještě nespustil žádné primitivum. |\n"
"| Úlohy session nejsou sledovány. | Session byla vytvořena z backendu jiné služby. Získej backend z `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| Logy workflow ukazují `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Workflow nemohl zaznamenat primitivní úlohu. Primitivní úloha stále běží, ale není sledována. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` ukazuje `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Klient nemohl z tvých lokálních přihlašovacích údajů vytvořit `QiskitRuntimeService`, proto zrušil pouze úlohu spravovaného workflow. |\n"
"| `client.job()` selže s `Job [...] not found`. | ID úlohy je špatné nebo úloha patří jinému uživateli. |\n"

